## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect per-tenant, private data path while supporting burst workloads, with per-tenant model versions, canary rollouts, and drift monitoring in AWS ML services.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint
- PrivateLink data residency
- Per-tenant Model Registry tags
- Canary rollouts and tenant routing
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo AWS SDK calls to register and route per-tenant models
const sm = new SageMaker({region: 'us-east-1'});
sm.registerModel({ModelName:'tenantA-v2', ...});
sm.createEndpoint({EndpointName:'multi-tenant-endpoint', ...});

// Lambda routing logic
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const tenant = event.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const modelName = `${tenant}-latest`;
  return await sm.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: 'multi-tenant-endpoint',
    TargetModel: modelName,
    Body: JSON.stringify(event.body)
  });
};
```
